From 4375f267ff780ee5ba52dd767a01d1d25baf650a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Sedgmen <dsedgmen@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:38:27 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 08/28] Make since_common.sh self-contained so it can be
 vendored

The CNV and ODF must-gather images ship their own collection scripts and need
the same window handling, but neither has a common.sh to source. Move
duration_to_seconds, duration_to_node_logs_since and get_since_cutoff out of
common.sh and into since_common.sh, and have common.sh source the library
instead. The dependency now runs one way, and the library stands alone.

Pure code movement; the 87 existing tests pass unchanged.

Also adds pod_tar_dirs_since, the multi-directory sibling of
copy_pod_dir_since, for collection that tars a fixed set of log directories
in one shot -- CNV collects QEMU logs with
`tar -cf - /var/log/libvirt/qemu/ /var/run/libvirt/qemu/log/ ...`, which has
no time bound at all.

hack/sync-since-lib.sh copies the canonical library into the sibling forks,
with --check for verifying rather than writing, so each fork can fail its
suite when its vendored copy has drifted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
